  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Kansas has $2.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, with 20,980 awards and an average award size of $127K. Obligations fell 25.4% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligating $1.5B, followed by the Department of Defense at $496M and the Department of Transportation at $462M. ORACLE HEALTH GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. is the largest vendor, receiving $1.3B, and INDRA AIR TRAFFIC, INC. follows with $381M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest industry by obligations at $1.3B, with Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $380M. Historical totals show obligations moving from $2.9B in FY21 up to $4.2B in FY22, then ranging between $3B and $3.6B through FY25 before the current FY26 to date total of $2.7B. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains the year-over-year change in obligations?",
        "body": "The statewide obligations fell 25.4% year over year, with total obligations at $2.7B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for $1.5B of obligations in the state, so shifts in VA buying would strongly affect the total. The Department of Defense obligated $496M and the Department of Transportation obligated $462M, making changes in those agencies also material to the statewide total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries dominate Kansas federal contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buying agency at $1.5B, followed by the Department of Defense at $496M and the Department of Transportation at $462M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest industry by obligations at $1.3B, and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing is second at $380M. ORACLE HEALTH GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. is the top vendor at $1.3B, with INDRA AIR TRAFFIC, INC. at $381M."
      }
    ]
  },
